## Model card

- **Name:** MAI-Code-1-Flash; distinct from successor MAI-Code-1.1-Flash.
- **Short description:** Microsoft coding model trained for GitHub Copilot's production harness.
- **Provider / access:** Released in the Copilot model/Auto picker; a separately supported public Chat Completions or Responses ID was not verified. No verified Zen Free ID.
- **Release / knowledge:** June 2, 2026; announcement updated June 8. Cutoff undisclosed.
- **Context / output:** No primary-source capacity or output limit verified in this research.
- **Modalities:** Coding and adaptive reasoning are documented; multimodal input and strict JSON capabilities unverified.
- **Architecture / license:** Proprietary; original model's parameter count not verified. Successor architecture is not transferred.
- **Pricing (2026-10-08):** Current per-token pricing for this exact original model not verified. [Microsoft announcement](https://microsoft.ai/news/introducingmai-code-1-flash/)
- **Availability:** GitHub lists retirement on September 10, 2026, recommending MAI-Code-1.1-Flash. [GitHub retirement history](https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/reference/ai-models/supported-models)

### Raw benchmarks found

- **Coding:** SWE-bench Pro **51.2%**, vendor evaluation in the production GitHub Copilot harness.
- **Reasoning:** Vendor's adversarial reasoning evaluation reports **85.8% adjusted accuracy**, across **186 questions / 34 categories**. This is an internal benchmark, not GPQA or HLE.
- **Efficiency:** Up to **60% fewer solution tokens** than Claude Haiku 4.5 in the vendor's SWE-bench Verified comparison; not a universal cost reduction.
[Original Microsoft release](https://microsoft.ai/news/introducingmai-code-1-flash/).
- Dedicated tool-use accuracy, numeric GPQA/HLE and long-context retrieval: no verified public score found in accessible primary text.
- Searches found inconsistent third-party context/pricing claims. Neither those claims nor the successor's specifications establish a complete original-model card.

### Normalized scores (1–100)

Not scored: coding and internal reasoning benchmarks are verified, but original-model context and current pricing could not be established from primary sources. Preserving evidence without inventing required dimensions; retirement alone is not the exclusion criterion.

